64: #!/usr/bin/env python3
65: """S4POST Stage B: project one frozen Web mount pack into ONE bounded fallback document.
66: 
67: There is no public directory listing for the plugin yet, so the current Web route is a single
68: markdown document a reader can attach to a conversation or a Knowledge base. This tool builds that
69: document from a *frozen mount pack* (a directory carrying ``MANIFEST.sha256``) and is fail-closed:
70: it REFUSES (typed reason, non-zero exit) rather than warn on
71: 
72:   * ``MANIFEST_DIGEST_MISMATCH``  a member's bytes no longer match ``MANIFEST.sha256``
73:   * ``MEMBER_SYMLINK``            a symlinked member (or pack) is present
74:   * ``PATH_ESCAPE``               a manifest path escapes the pack root
75:   * ``UNEXPECTED_EXTRA_FILE``     a file exists in the pack that the manifest does not list
76:   * ``RELEASE_STAMP_MISSING``     a member document does not stamp the release commit
77:   * ``SIZE_CAP_EXCEEDED``         the composed document would exceed the cap (NEVER truncated)
78:   * ``DESTINATION_EXISTS`` / ``DESTINATION_SYMLINK``  the output file already exists
79: 
80: The document is written with ``O_EXCL`` and stamps ``DOC_MOUNT_ONLY`` plus the member inventory. No
81: timestamp is embedded, so two builds are byte-identical.
82: 
83: CLI
84: ---
85: ``--mount-pack DIR``      unpacked frozen mount pack (contains MANIFEST.sha256)
86: ``--release-id TEXT``     e.g. v0.1.1-preview.3 (informational stamp)
87: ``--release-commit HEX40`` the commit the members must stamp
88: ``--size-cap BYTES``      hard cap for the composed document (default 524288)
89: ``--out FILE``            destination markdown file (must not exist)
90: """
