193: ### G. External and human gates
194: 
195: - Vendor's own manifest validator: NOT_EXECUTED — only the repository's local validator and synthetic tests were run; no vendor validator was invoked.
196: - OpenAI Portal scan/review: NOT_EXECUTED — no Portal submission, scan receipt, or review was performed.
197: - Real Host effective-load beyond this machine: NOT_EXECUTED — no external host was installed or exercised.
198: - codex-desktop GUI: NOT_EXECUTED — no GUI load/install/use acceptance flow was operated.
199: - Claude Code: NOT_EXECUTED — no Claude Code runtime or integration was launched.
200: - Windows account UAT: NOT_EXECUTED — unattended unit tests under this process are not a user/account UAT.
201: - GitHub Actions workflow execution: NOT_EXECUTED — the workflow was inspected locally; a remote run was not started or certified.
202: - Real filesystem symlink-overwrite attempt: NOT_EXECUTED — os.symlink failed with OSError(22, '用戶端沒有這項特殊權限。'); a real hardlink attack WAS executed instead.
203: 
204: ## Findings
205: 
206: ### AO-01 — HIGH — An output hardlink permits sentinel overwrite despite F05 closure language
207: 
208: Claim: the coverage matrix calls F05 'symlink overwrote a sentinel' REPAIRED and identifies 'check_output_root + O_EXCL test_05, test_21-path case'.
209: 
210: Exact falsifying command, with TEMP/TMP/TMPDIR=AO/temp and PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1:
211: 
212: ~~~text
213: python AO/probe_f05.py
214: ~~~
215: 
216: The harness imports the candidate's existing complete-owner fixture and invokes its REAL Env.build -> build_plugin. No candidate code is patched. It precreates the checksum output as a real hardlink to a sentinel outside the output directory; all attack files remain inside AO/temp. Raw output:
217: 
218: ~~~text
219: symlink: NOT_EXECUTED link creation failed: OSError(22, '用戶端沒有這項特殊權限。')
220: hardlink: before=b'INDEPENDENT_AO_SENTINEL_DO_NOT_OVERWRITE\n'
221: hardlink: builder_verdict=BUILT
222: hardlink: after=b'e77501f25007ceb96d3e107070ad6d223731a07b51c04fcfdfb1b2676df918a6  pipd-ls-sp-public-skills.zip\n'
223: hardlink: sentinel_untouched=False
224: probe_exit=0
225: ~~~
226: 
227: Evidence: probe_f05.py and D_f05_probe_raw.txt. tools/build_public_plugin.py:800 writes sidecar bytes non-exclusively; lines 804–805 likewise write mapping/receipt paths. Root/ancestor symlink rejection does not protect pre-existing output members. The measured attack is a HARDLINK, not a successfully created symlink; it establishes an actual unauthorized overwrite in the complete-owner fixture, not that today's owner-missing release configuration can produce a real archive. The local attacker must be able to prepopulate the output directory/link. No TOCTOU exploitation, production attacker access, or vendor-host behavior was measured.
228: 
229: ### AO-02 — MEDIUM — Delivered-tree clean precondition is false
230: 
231: Claim: the candidate must be clean. Exact falsifying command: git -C T status --porcelain, run before AO output creation. Raw initial status is under Subject and shows three pre-existing untracked stage-b files. The subsequent freeze refuses DIRTY_WORKTREE, not the owner gate. This is a delivery/environment finding, not a tracked-code mutation. The remote commit itself matches.
232: 
233: ### AO-03 — MEDIUM — CI's write-set guard is narrower than the required upgrade allowlist
234: 
235: Claim under challenge: the workflow guard matches the stated upgrade set and protects dist as well as frozen paths. Exact inspection/falsification commands:
236: 
237: ~~~text
238: Get-Content .github/workflows/public-plugin-verify.yml
239: foreach($path in @('dist/payload.zip','unrelated/changed.txt','docs/elsewhere.md','skills/pipd-route-intake/SKILL.md')) { Write-Output "path=$path rejected_by_workflow_guard=$($path -match '^(skills|src|schemas)/')" }
240: ~~~
241: 
242: Raw evaluation (DF_detail_raw.txt):
243: 
244: ~~~text
245: path=dist/payload.zip rejected_by_workflow_guard=False
246: path=unrelated/changed.txt rejected_by_workflow_guard=False
247: path=docs/elsewhere.md rejected_by_workflow_guard=False
248: path=skills/pipd-route-intake/SKILL.md rejected_by_workflow_guard=True
249: ~~~
250: 
251: The guard only rejects ^(skills|src|schemas)/. It has no positive allowed-path check and no dist exclusion. It derives BASE from PR base or HEAD~1, not from the fixed stacked base. A workflow_dispatch run on this commit defaults to the immediately preceding commit, so it does not necessarily examine the entire stacked Stage-B write set. This is a guard-logic mismatch; I did NOT execute a mutated remote CI run. The independently measured committed diff nevertheless has zero violations.
252: 
253: ### D. Historical test coverage assessment (F01–F05)
254: 
255: All methods below belong to PublicPluginPackagingTest in tests/test_public_plugin_packaging.py. Entire source is preserved in C_preflight_raw.txt; targeted excerpts in D_sources_raw.txt and DF_detail_raw.txt. Their executions are included in the 44 passing focused cases.
256: 
257: | Defect | Method(s) | What the test actually does | Scope assessment |
258: |---|---|---|---|
259: | F01 fake PNG accepted | test_01_png_signature_with_broken_body_is_refused; test_01_non_png_icon_is_refused | Replaces real fixture icon bytes, supplies matching malicious digest, invokes real builder, checks ICON_INVALID and motive (truncated_chunk/signature), checks no output. | Direct regression inputs, not vacuous. Does not establish every PNG validity rule or Portal scanning. |
260: | F02 arbitrary manifest accepted | test_02_unknown_manifest_property_is_refused; test_16_unknown_top_level_key_in_the_official_manifest_is_refused; test_16_the_previous_internal_manifest_is_refused_as_the_package_root | Inserts unknown keys / legacy root shape into packaging fixtures and checks exact real-builder schema refusal. | Direct local schema regression, not vacuous. Local validate_subset and byte-pinned schema are NOT execution of the vendor's own validator. |
261: | F03 invalid SKILL.md accepted | test_03_skill_without_frontmatter_is_refused; test_03_skill_with_wrong_frontmatter_name_is_refused; test_12_complete_owner_record_builds_and_projects_the_body_verbatim | Freezes the malformed source first (preventing a hash-drift proxy), invokes real builder, checks SKILL_FRONTMATTER_INVALID; positive case checks body and kept/dropped keys in a built zip. | Direct missing-frontmatter/name regressions with a real positive build. Not exhaustive vendor skill-format qualification. |
262: | F04 null source_commit accepted | test_04_source_commit_gates | Calls real builder with None, abc123 and a differing 40-hex value; checks SOURCE_COMMIT_NULL/INVALID/MISMATCH and no zip. | Direct regression at Python API boundary. Does not separately execute a subprocess CLI omitting --source-commit in this method. |
263: | F05 symlink overwrote sentinel | test_05_symlinked_output_root_is_refused_and_target_untouched | Makes the OUTPUT ROOT a symlink, or substitutes only _path_is_symlink if Windows disallows it; checks OUTPUT_ROOT_SYMLINK, sentinel bytes, and directory members. | Genuine root gate test, but on this machine it exercises a predicate seam, not real filesystem symlink resolution. A proxy for generalized overwrite safety; does not test output-member symlinks/hardlinks or concurrent swaps. AO-01 actually overwrites a sentinel through a hardlink. |
264: 
265: No listed test was found to be vacuous or to assert an unrelated refusal code. F05 is materially narrower than the closure language. Exact additional inspection: rg -n '^    def test_(05|21)' tests/test_public_plugin_packaging.py. The frozen module has test_05 but no test_21; the coverage matrix's test_21-path locator cannot be resolved there. mkstemp's exclusive temporary zip creation does not make the subsequent sidecar/receipt writes exclusive.
266: 
267: ### F. CI workflow inspection
268: 
269: - Actual triggers: pull_request with path filters and workflow_dispatch; no push trigger.
270: - Permissions block: contents: read; checkout specifies persist-credentials: false. No explicit repository-push/tag/publish command or write-token permission was found.
271: - Literal pull_request_target DOES appear, in the comment on line 9; it is NOT a YAML trigger. Likewise secrets.* appears in that comment, not a secret-consuming expression. A literal 'nowhere in the file' claim would be false; absence of that active trigger is supported by inspection.
272: - No step explicitly needs a configured secret. This is a source inspection, not proof of every third-party action's implementation or all code executed by pip install/tests.
273: - Steps CAN and DO write to the runner's checkout: py_compile writes bytecode; pip's editable installation/test suite has writes; the mutation step rewrites a tracked dist/mount README then git checkout restores it; logs and fallback work files are created. Therefore 'no repository write' is defensible only as NO REMOTE GITHUB REPOSITORY MUTATION, not as a read-only local worktree promise.
274: - Path filters include docs/RELEASE_TUPLE.json and dist/mount/**, which are outside the user-specified upgrade set, while omitting broad tools/tests, docs/adr, OpenSpec and round-evidence paths. 'restricted to the upgrade paths' in the header is not an exact description of this task's allowlist.
275: - docs/install/README.md:165 calls it a 'read-only gate'; that wording needs the remote-versus-local distinction. The file/docs explicitly deny Portal/publication/host/S4 acceptance; those ceilings are appropriately stated, not independently granted here.
276: - Guard/base discrepancies and measured regex evidence are in AO-03. Entire workflow and documentation search output: F_workflow_raw.txt.
277: 
278: ## Verdict
279: 
280: **FAIL_CHALLENGE**
281: 
282: Scope: the measured local challenge of commit 2a903bd09c7760c494f20ed98b840fae789b24d6 finds an actual complete-owner-fixture output hardlink overwrite and a CI guard mismatch; it also records a dirty delivered tree and a non-passing isolated 569-test run. It DOES NOT authorize release, merge, publish, or S4 full pass, and does not cover vendor/Portal/GUI/other-host/account UAT or an original-tree full-suite execution.
283: 
284: Passing subclaims remain passing: requested commit/remote readback, eight/48 ledger inventory and hashes, stacked-base zero-outside-path diff, unchanged skills subtree, 44 focused tests, and owner refusal/no archive in the clean isolated copy. A FAIL_CHALLENGE is not a claim that every candidate feature failed.
285: 
286: ## Makers-vs-checker differences
287: 
288: - Maker totals 44 and 569: measured totals match; 44 is green, while the isolated 569 run exits 1 with 4 failures, 3 errors and 6 skips. Original-tree full-suite execution remains NOT_EXECUTED under the hard write prohibition; local-copy environmental effects prevent a clean regression attribution.
289: - Clean subject assumption: false before checker outputs existed; three untracked stage-b files were already present.
290: - Requested local branch identity: local branch lacks -r2; remote -r2 and local HEAD nevertheless resolve to the specified commit.
291: - Real owner refusal: not reached in the requested original freeze/build chain (dirty tree, then missing ledger). Reproduced only in a separate clean committed copy after copy-local longpath configuration. Refusal text is stdout, not stderr.
292: - F05 'REPAIRED' coverage: root symlink refusal passes, but generalized sentinel safety does not; real hardlink overwrite measured. Matrix's test_21-path locator is absent from the packaging test module.
293: - CI 'read-only'/'upgrade paths' wording: no explicit remote write step, but runner checkout writes and the guard/filter set is not the required allowlist. Remote CI execution NOT_EXECUTED.
294: - All external/human qualification gates remain NOT_EXECUTED. This report grants none of them.
