     1	#!/usr/bin/env bash
     2	# Governed lane launcher - fixes the recurring handover-hygiene defect.
     3	#
     4	# Root cause it addresses: the previous runners wrote the brief, the runner itself and the lane log
     5	# INTO the same worktree that was then handed to the officer. The delivery was therefore dirty by
     6	# construction, and two independent officers correctly refused to call it clean.
     7	#
     8	# This wrapper enforces five things:
     9	#   1. FAIL-CLOSED preflight: the worktree must be clean before an officer is launched against it.
    10	#   2. Harness artifacts under the round directory are COMMITTED before launch, not left untracked.
    11	#   3. The lane log is written OUTSIDE the worktree (system temp), so the log cannot dirty the delivery.
    12	#   4. The officer's own output directory is created before launch and is the only permitted dirt.
    13	#   5. Postflight: copy the log in, commit the lane artifacts, and assert the worktree is clean again.
    14	#
    15	# usage: run_lane.sh <lanelupper> <brief-basename> <in-round-output-subdir> [model]
    16	#   e.g. run_lane.sh AO4 VERIFIER_AO4_BRIEF.md verify/ao4
    17	set -u
    18	# The worktree is overridable so the refusal path can be tested in an external clone by a checker,
    19	# without ever dirtying the real delivery.
